\details{
Method parameters are attached automatically to every chromatogram and
peak table read from these files, in the \code{method_params} metadata field.
This includes all scalar values but leaves out the oven program, gradient
and other tables, which are only returned by this function. The \code{ms} module
of a GC-MS or LC-MS run is attached as \code{ms_params}.
}
\section{File format}{

\code{.gcd} and \code{.lcd} files store the method and instrument configuration as
labeled XML, in the \code{GUC.1.METHOD} and \code{GUC.1.CONFIG} streams, and the PDA
settings in \code{PDA.1.METHOD}. The settings of a single or triple quadrupole
mass spectrometer are records stored as hex in the same XML, in the
\code{LCMS} unit of its own \code{GUC.1.METHOD} or \code{GUM.METHOD} stream; of these,
only the interface record (\code{Ifs}) is read, whose DL and heat block
temperatures are uint16 in hundredths of a degree at bytes 70 and 74.
They were checked against a method printout for an 'LCMS-2020' and the
published method of an 'LCMS-8040'.

\code{.qgd} files from a GC-2030 (e.g. with a 'GCMS-QP2020 NX') also hold the GC
method and configuration as labeled XML, in \verb{GCMS Configuration/GUC_GC2},
and their oven, injector, autosampler and column settings are read from it
as for \code{.gcd} files. Every \code{.qgd} file stores the method as unlabeled binary
records, one stream per module, at fixed byte offsets, which are read for the
other settings and for files without the XML. Values are little-endian
float32 unless marked otherwise, and bytes not listed are not read. The same
streams are found in files from 'GCMS-QP2010' and 'QP2020 NX' instruments:
\itemize{
\item \verb{GC-2010 Instrument Parameters/Column Oven Parameter}, 260 bytes:
\itemize{
\item 8: the number of ramps, n (int32).
\item 12, 16: the initial temperature and hold.
\item 20, 100, 180: the rates, target temperatures and holds, each an array of
20 slots, of which those past n are zero.
}
\item \verb{GC-2010 Instrument Parameters/Injection Parameter-1}, 512 bytes:
\itemize{
\item 12, 16, 20: the column flow, linear velocity and split ratio.
\item 24, 120, 216, 312: the temperature, total flow, pressure and purge flow
programs, 96 bytes each: the number of ramps (int32), the initial value
and hold, then arrays of 7 rates, targets and holds.
}
\item \verb{GCMS Configuration/Column-1}, 832 bytes:
\itemize{
\item 0, 64: the column name and serial number, null-terminated strings of up
to 64 bytes.
\item 132: the length in tenths of a metre (int32).
\item 140: the maximum temperature (int32).
}
\item \verb{QP5K Instrument Parameters/MS Parameter}, 600 or 664 bytes:
\itemize{
\item 20: the ion source temperature in tenths of a degree (int32).
\item 44, 48: the start and end of acquisition in milliseconds (int32).
\item 52: the event time in milliseconds (int32).
}
}

The interface temperature is only read from the XML, as the additional
heater the configuration names \code{MS}. Method heaters are numbered by their
position in the configuration's list of heaters, which starts at 2, so the
\code{MS} heater is method heater 4 in every file seen.

The settings were checked against the 'GCMSsolution' method printouts
published with three 'QP2020 NX' runs.
}

